{% comment %}
  One-time purchase, shown under the subscription options.

  Two shapes, from one setting. As a Link it is the quiet escape hatch it has
  always been. As a Card it borrows the offer card's chrome and sits in the
  stack looking like one more option — which is what a product whose real choice
  is "once or monthly" wants, without one-time having to become a selling plan
  it is not.

  Two behaviours, likewise. Add Immediately keeps the original contract: the
  click clears the selling plan, sets quantity to 1 and submits the form, so the
  plain product goes to the cart on its own. Select Only makes it a selection
  and nothing more — the plan is cleared and the card marked, and the shopper
  presses Add To Cart themselves.

  Card + Add Immediately is a deliberate combination, not an accident: it looks
  like a radio and behaves like a button. Pair Card with Select Only when the
  card sits among selectable plans, which is the case it was added for.

  Supply is a product option on NanoGreens, so clearing the plan is only half of
  it — without a supply of its own this would add whichever supply card was last
  selected, which reads to a shopper as the choice being ignored. Supply Option
  Value names the size a one-time purchase is, and the script resolves it against
  the flavour the shopper is on rather than pinning a variant, so the flavour
  survives. Left blank the previously selected variant stands, which is right for
  every product whose supply is not an option.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the onetime block. Reads settings.text, settings.style,
    settings.behavior, settings.sublabel, settings.show_price,
    settings.supply_value.
  - product {Object} - product being sold; blank in preview.
  - current_variant {Object} - variant whose price is quoted on the card.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-onetime__block',
    block: block,
    product: product,
    current_variant: current_variant
  %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign onetime_style = block.settings.style | default: 'link'
  assign onetime_behavior = block.settings.behavior | default: 'add_immediately'
-%}

{%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
  {%- if onetime_style == 'card' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      A button, not a label with a radio inside it. The radio in an offer card
      belongs to the supply group, and putting a real one here would let the
      browser's own group behaviour fight the script over which option is live —
      on Add Immediately there is no selection to hold at all. The radio dot is
      drawn instead, off the same class the real cards use so the two are
      indistinguishable.

      The card wears __offer and __offer--selected but carries none of the
      data-cwc-offer* attributes, and that separation is load-bearing rather than
      an omission. The script looks the live selection up by the selected class,
      so this card is found — and then every attribute it reads off it comes back
      empty, which is exactly right: no plan, no add-on, and a price that falls
      back to the variant's own. Giving this card data-cwc-offer-now or
      data-cwc-offer-plan would quietly make it behave like a subscription.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer cwc_product-hero-buy-box__onetime-card"
      data-cwc-onetime
      data-cwc-onetime-label="{{ block.settings.text | escape }}"
      data-cwc-onetime-card
      data-cwc-onetime-behavior="{{ onetime_behavior }}"
      {% if block.settings.supply_value != blank %}
        data-cwc-onetime-value="{{ block.settings.supply_value | strip | escape }}"
      {% endif %}
      {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
    >
      <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-body">
        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-name">{{ block.settings.text }}</span>

        {% if block.settings.sublabel != blank %}
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-description">{{ block.settings.sublabel }}</span>
        {% endif %}

        {%- comment -%}
          The variant's own price, not a plan's. It follows the option pickers
          through the same data attribute the offer cards use, so a size change
          re-prices this card along with the rest.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% if block.settings.show_price and current_variant != blank %}
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-price">
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-now" data-cwc-onetime-price>
              {{- current_variant.price | money -}}
            </span>
            {% if current_variant.compare_at_price > current_variant.price %}
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-was" data-cwc-onetime-compare>
                {{- current_variant.compare_at_price | money -}}
              </span>
            {% endif %}
          </span>
        {% endif %}
      </span>
    </button>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__onetime" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__onetime-button"
        data-cwc-onetime
        data-cwc-onetime-label="{{ block.settings.text | escape }}"
        data-cwc-onetime-behavior="{{ onetime_behavior }}"
        {% if block.settings.supply_value != blank %}
          data-cwc-onetime-value="{{ block.settings.supply_value | strip | escape }}"
        {% endif %}
      >
        {{ block.settings.text }}
        {% if block.settings.show_price and current_variant != blank %}
          <span data-cwc-onetime-price>{{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </button>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
